  "lineage": "Popular entertainment bands of Māori musicians that grew from the concert-party tradition and toured New Zealand, Australia, Asia and the United States from the late 1950s into the 1970s, combining close-harmony singing, electric band backing and comedy with Māori songs and action songs and current pop and show tunes. The Howard Morrison Quartet recorded hits for La Gloria, and the Maori Volcanics, Quin Tikis and Maori Hi-Five were leading touring showbands.",
